WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.412
This example creates a diagnosis summary as a materialized view.

00:00:04.412 --> 00:00:07.677
One row represents one diagnosis.

00:00:07.677 --> 00:00:15.382
The stored measures include the number of admissions, the number of distinct patients, and the average length of stay.

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:21.887
The example also stores a refresh time so we can see when the snapshot was generated.

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:27.942
That refresh time does not change simply because someone queries the materialized view.

00:00:27.942 --> 00:00:30.966
It changes when the stored result is rebuilt.
